 },
 "method": "2026-10-15, through the public CMNPD site in a browser (the cloud network cannot reach cmnpd.org): each species was searched by its WoRMS accepted name and every WoRMS synonym (the names of research/verified-indices/snapshots/mbpi-links-2026-09-30.json); an exact organism match gave the organism ID, and its 'Associated Compounds' list gave the compound IDs. For each compound the standard InChIKey and CMNPD's own ChEMBL cross-reference were read to compare with the MBPI species -> compound links (Wikidata P703 + original-paper links of verified-4.18). Only CMNPD IDs and match results are stored here; compound names, structures, InChIKeys and activity values are not redistributed.",
 "match_rule": "mbpi_link: same_inchikey = the MBPI link set of the species holds the same standard InChIKey; same_skeleton = only the first InChIKey block (connectivity) matches, so a stereo or charge variant, not the same compound; none = no MBPI link. mbpi_chembl_id = the ChEMBL parent of a same_inchikey MBPI link (null when the MBPI link has no ChEMBL molecule). cmnpd_chembl_xref = the ChEMBL ID CMNPD lists for the compound; each one was looked up in ChEMBL on 2026-10-15 and its InChIKey equals the CMNPD one.",
 "reference_check": {
  "organism": "Conus magus",
  "result": "not in CMNPD 1.0 (no organism match for Conus magus; ziconotide and conotoxin have no CMNPD entry). The Conus magus-type gap (compound in ChEMBL, species link missing) is therefore counted inside the 30 species with CMNPD's ChEMBL cross-references."
 },
